      "writtenOn": "2026-11-05T20:54:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "val[0] bits 4:2 (AW) stores the stage-2 paging depth, while stage-1\u0027s paging depth is stored in val[2] bits 3:2 (FLPM: 0 \u003d 4-level / agaw 2, 1 \u003d 5-level / agaw 3):\n\n- For SL_ONLY and non-pKVM NESTED, debugfs walks the S2 table in val[0] (SLPTPTR), so AW in val[0] matches it.\n- For FL_ONLY, debugfs walks the S1 table in val[2] (FLPTPTR), so strictly speaking it should read FLPM too - line 432 only works for FL DMA domains by coincidence because pasid_pte_config_first_level() writes iommu-\u003eagaw into AW, which happens to match domain-\u003eagaw (for SVA it can actually mismatch, e.g. 4-level CPU paging on a 5-level IOMMU).\n- For pKVM NESTED, debugfs walks the host\u0027s S1 table in val[2] (since S2 is pKVM\u0027s inaccessible host EPT), while pasid_pte_config_nestd() sets AW in val[0] to pt_domain.agaw (from pkvm_host_ept_level()). Since the host EPT level can differ from S1\u0027s level (iommu-\u003eagaw), we need to read FLPM from val[2] here.",
      "parentUuid": "96bfc6b4_2958dc0e",
      "revId": "86298094326a14943e613f90381acf7702ba46e3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
