      "message": "I see, thanks for the details.\n\n\u003e For FL_ONLY, debugfs walks the S1 table in val[2] (FLPTPTR), so strictly speaking it should read FLPM too - line 432 only works for FL DMA domains by coincidence because pasid_pte_config_first_level() writes iommu-\u003eagaw into AW, which happens to match domain-\u003eagaw (for SVA it can actually mismatch, e.g. 4-level CPU paging on a 5-level IOMMU).\n\nI see. This is actually what I was wondering about: why is the PASID_ENTRY_PGTT_FL_ONLY case using agaw if it is for SL only. (And why does pasid_pte_config_first_level() set agaw if it is for SL only?)\n\nSo, we have an actual upstream bug here (at least due to the SVA case)?",
