      "writtenOn": "2026-11-05T20:54:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`iommu_iotlb_gather_init()` initializes an empty gather to `start \u003d ULONG_MAX, end \u003d 0`, and in 6.18 `iommu_iotlb_sync()` still calls `-\u003eiotlb_sync()` unconditionally on empty gathers (e.g. if iommu_unmap() hits a non-present PTE and unmaps 0 bytes, or on 0-size error unwinds in `iommu_map`), which would pass `[ULONG_MAX, 0]` to `pkvm_domain_flush()` and hit -EINVAL.\n\nUpstream fixed this generically in iommu_iotlb_sync() in `commit 90c5def10bea (\"iommu: Do not call drivers for empty gathers\")`, which now I have backported in this series as aosp/4420121",
      "parentUuid": "4773ca1e_cc9b6778",
      "revId": "86298094326a14943e613f90381acf7702ba46e3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
